# Multi-tenant routing: tenant and schoolYear are PATH segments (/mt-dms/{tenant}/{schoolYear}),
# and a token only reaches the data store its application is bound to. A token used on another
# tenant's path is answered 404 ("No database instance found matching the request route
# qualifiers"), not 401/403: DMS matches the token's data store against the route and finds none.
#
# Credentials: the tenant1 and tenant2 API clients from bootstrap.ps1 output.
# Re-running: the first POST of a record returns 201; later runs return 200 (upsert).

@base = https://your-label.eastus.cloudapp.azure.com
@realm = edfi
@schoolYear = 2025

# The raw `Basic key:secret` form below is base64-encoded automatically by VS Code REST Client.
# Pre-encode it instead (`Authorization: Basic <base64(key:secret)>`) if a secret contains
# characters REST Client treats as variables ({{ }}) or your client does not auto-encode the raw form.
@tenant1Key = REPLACE_WITH_TENANT1_KEY
@tenant1Secret = REPLACE_WITH_TENANT1_SECRET
@tenant2Key = REPLACE_WITH_TENANT2_KEY
@tenant2Secret = REPLACE_WITH_TENANT2_SECRET

### Get a token for tenant1
# @name tokenRequestOne
POST {{base}}/auth/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Authorization: Basic {{tenant1Key}}:{{tenant1Secret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

###
@tokenOne = {{tokenRequestOne.response.body.access_token}}

### Get a token for tenant2
# @name tokenRequestTwo
POST {{base}}/auth/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Authorization: Basic {{tenant2Key}}:{{tenant2Secret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

###
@tokenTwo = {{tokenRequestTwo.response.body.access_token}}

### Create a person with the tenant1 token. Note tenant1 in the URL. ALLOWED (201, or 200 on re-run).
POST {{base}}/mt-dms/tenant1/{{schoolYear}}/data/ed-fi/people
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personId": "security-review-one",
  "sourceSystemDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/SourceSystemDescriptor#District"
}

### Same person, same URL, but the tenant2 token. DENIED (404): this token routes only to tenant2's data store.
POST {{base}}/mt-dms/tenant1/{{schoolYear}}/data/ed-fi/people
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTwo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personId": "security-review-one",
  "sourceSystemDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/SourceSystemDescriptor#District"
}

### Try again with tenant2's URL. ALLOWED (201, or 200 on re-run).
POST {{base}}/mt-dms/tenant2/{{schoolYear}}/data/ed-fi/people
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTwo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personId": "security-review-one",
  "sourceSystemDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/SourceSystemDescriptor#District"
}

### Read with the tenant1 token
GET {{base}}/mt-dms/tenant1/{{schoolYear}}/data/ed-fi/people?personId=security-review-one
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}

### Read with the tenant2 token. A different record in a different database: compare `id` and `_lastModifiedDate`.
GET {{base}}/mt-dms/tenant2/{{schoolYear}}/data/ed-fi/people?personId=security-review-one
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTwo}}

### Read tenant2's data with the tenant1 token. DENIED (404).
GET {{base}}/mt-dms/tenant2/{{schoolYear}}/data/ed-fi/people?personId=security-review-one
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}

### Right tenant, but a school year with no data store. DENIED (404).
GET {{base}}/mt-dms/tenant1/2099/data/ed-fi/people?personId=security-review-one
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}
